{%- comment -%}
  product-card — one product tile. The most reused markup on the site.

  Used by featured-collection and main-collection, and by main-product /
  product-recommendations when those are built. It is a snippet, not a section,
  precisely so those cannot drift apart.

  Parameters:
    product      — required
    loading      — 'eager' for the first row above the fold, otherwise 'lazy'
    sizes        — the sizes attribute for the grid it sits in
    show_type    — show the product type as an eyebrow. Default true.
    price_prefix — force the price wording: 'setting' | 'from' | 'none'.
                   Omit it and the card works the wording out itself; see below.

  THE CARD, per the design system: squared image, uppercase eyebrow, Outfit
  name, £ price. No border, no shadow — whitespace and the image edge do the
  separating. Hover shifts the name to sage and gently scales the image; if the
  product has a second image, it cross-fades to it instead, which for rings is
  usually the on-hand shot.

  Money is always `| money`, never a hand-built string with a £ in it — the
  store is GBP today, and a hardcoded symbol is how that becomes a bug later.

  PRICE WORDING — three cases, decided from the product, not the page.
  Ed's rule, 31/08/2026:

    loose stones (diamonds, gemstones)   the actual price
    engagement rings                     "Setting from <price>"
    wedding, eternity, plain bands       "From <price>"

  Rather than key that to collection handles — which would be wrong the moment
  a ring appears in search, on the ring pages, or in a featured row — it is
  derived from what the product IS:

    · a product whose price does not vary has ONE price, so it states it. A
      loose stone is a single SKU, which is exactly this case.
    · a ring that varies and is tagged 'Engagement Ring' says "Setting from",
      because the stone is chosen separately and "From" would understate by an
      order of magnitude.
    · anything else that varies says "From" — the variation is metal and size,
      which is a modest spread.

  The tag is the same one the Engagement Rings collection is built on, so the
  card and the collection cannot disagree. `price_prefix` overrides all of it
  where a caller knows better.

  Price logic, in the order it is decided:
    sold out            → "Sold out", no price
    on sale             → sale price, then the original struck through
    varies by variant   → the prefix above, then the lowest price
    otherwise           → the price
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign show_eyebrow = show_type
  if show_type == nil
    assign show_eyebrow = true
  endif
  assign img_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign img_sizes = sizes | default: '(max-width: 560px) 50vw, (max-width: 900px) 33vw, 25vw'
  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif
  assign second = product.images[1]
  assign card_alt = product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title

  comment
    Resolve the wording once. `price_prefix` from the caller wins; otherwise
    the tag decides. Only consulted when the price actually varies.
  endcomment
  assign prefix_mode = price_prefix
  if prefix_mode == blank
    if product.tags contains 'Engagement Ring'
      assign prefix_mode = 'setting'
    else
      assign prefix_mode = 'from'
    endif
  endif

  assign price_lead = ''
  if prefix_mode == 'setting'
    assign price_lead = 'Setting from '
  elsif prefix_mode == 'from'
    assign price_lead = 'From '
  endif
-%}

<div class="pcard">
  <a class="pcard__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
    <span class="pcard__media">
      {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
        {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag:
           loading: img_loading,
           widths: '200,300,400,600,900',
           sizes: img_sizes,
           alt: card_alt,
           class: 'pcard__img' }}
        {%- if second != blank -%}
          {{ second | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag:
             loading: 'lazy',
             widths: '200,300,400,600,900',
             sizes: img_sizes,
             alt: '',
             class: 'pcard__img pcard__img--alt' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="pcard__ph"></span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless product.available -%}
        <span class="pcard__badge">Sold out</span>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <span class="pcard__badge">Sale</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    </span>

    <span class="pcard__words">
      {%- if show_eyebrow and product.type != blank -%}
        <span class="pcard__type">{{ product.type }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <span class="pcard__name">{{ product.title }}</span>

      <span class="pcard__price">
        {%- if product.available == false -%}
          <span class="pcard__sold">Sold out</span>
        {%- elsif on_sale -%}
          <span class="pcard__now">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
          <s class="pcard__was">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
        {%- elsif product.price_varies -%}
          <span class="pcard__now">{{ price_lead }}{{ product.price_min | money }}</span>
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="pcard__now">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </span>
  </a>
</div>
